{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01C5sREJLaATAXFiauZjZ4hv","type":"tool_result","content":"330\t}\n331\t\n332\t\n333\t\n334\t/*************************************************\n335\t*          Match a back-reference                *\n336\t*************************************************/\n337\t\n338\t/* This function is called only when it is known that the offset lies within\n339\tthe offsets that have so far been used in the match. Note that in caseless\n340\tUTF-8 mode, the number of subject bytes matched may be different to the number\n341\tof reference bytes. (In theory this could also happen in UTF-16 mode, but it\n342\tseems unlikely.)\n343\t\n344\tArguments:\n345\t  offset      index into the offset vector\n346\t  caseless    TRUE if caseless\n347\t  caseopts    bitmask of REFI_FLAG_XYZ values\n348\t  F           the current backtracking frame pointer\n349\t  mb          points to match block\n350\t  lengthptr   pointer for returning the length matched\n351\t\n352\tReturns:      = 0 sucessful match; number of code units matched is set\n353\t              < 0 no match\n354\t              > 0 partial match\n355\t*/\n356\t\n357\tstatic int\n358\tmatch_ref(PCRE2_SIZE offset, BOOL caseless, int caseopts, heapframe *F,\n359\t  match_block *mb, PCRE2_SIZE *lengthptr)\n360\t{\n361\tPCRE2_SPTR p;\n362\tPCRE2_SIZE length;\n363\tPCRE2_SPTR eptr;\n364\tPCRE2_SPTR eptr_start;\n365\t\n366\t#ifndef SUPPORT_UNICODE\n367\t(void)caseopts; /* Avoid compiler warning. */\n368\t#endif\n369\t\n370\t/* Deal with an unset group. The default is no match, but there is an option to\n371\tmatch an empty string. */\n372\t\n373\tif (offset >= Foffset_top || Fovector[offset] == PCRE2_UNSET)\n374\t  {\n375\t  if ((mb->poptions & PCRE2_MATCH_UNSET_BACKREF) != 0)\n376\t    {\n377\t    *lengthptr = 0;\n378\t    return 0;      /* Match */\n379\t    }\n380\t  else return -1;  /* No match */\n381\t  }\n382\t\n383\t/* Separate the caseless and UTF cases for speed. */\n384\t\n385\teptr = eptr_start = Feptr;\n386\tp = mb->start_subject + Fovector[offset];\n387\tlength = Fovector[offset+1] - Fovector[offset];\n388\tPCRE2_ASSERT(eptr <= mb->end_subject);\n389\t\n390\tif (caseless)\n391\t  {\n392\t#if defined SUPPORT_UNICODE\n393\t  BOOL utf = (mb->poptions & PCRE2_UTF) != 0;\n394\t  BOOL caseless_restrict = (caseopts & REFI_FLAG_CASELESS_RESTRICT) != 0;\n395\t  BOOL turkish_casing = !caseless_restrict && (caseopts & REFI_FLAG_TURKISH_CASING) != 0;\n396\t\n397\t  if (utf || (mb->poptions & PCRE2_UCP) != 0)\n398\t    {\n399\t    PCRE2_SPTR endptr = p + length;\n400\t\n401\t    /* Match characters up to the end of the reference. NOTE: the number of\n402\t    code units matched may differ, because in UTF-8 there are some characters\n403\t    whose upper and lower case codes have different numbers of bytes. For\n404\t    example, U+023A (2 bytes in UTF-8) is the upper case version of U+2C65 (3\n405\t    bytes in UTF-8); a sequence of 3 of the former uses 6 bytes, as does a\n406\t    sequence of two of the latter. It is important, therefore, to check the\n407\t    length along the reference, not along the subject (earlier code did this\n408\t    wrong). UCP uses Unicode properties but without UTF encoding. */\n409\t\n410\t    while (p < endptr)\n411\t      {\n412\t      uint32_t c, d;\n413\t      const ucd_record *ur;\n414\t      if (eptr >= mb->end_subject) return 1;   /* Partial match */\n415\t\n416\t      if (utf)\n417\t        {\n418\t        GETCHARINC(c, eptr);\n419\t        GETCHARINC(d, p);\n420\t        }\n421\t      else\n422\t        {\n423\t        c = *eptr++;\n424\t        d = *p++;\n425\t        }\n426\t\n427\t      if (turkish_casing && UCD_ANY_I(d))\n428\t        {\n429\t        c = UCD_FOLD_I_TURKISH(c);\n430\t        d = UCD_FOLD_I_TURKISH(d);\n431\t        if (c != d) return -1;  /* No match */\n432\t        }\n433\t      else if (c != d && c != (uint32_t)((int)d + (ur = GET_UCD(d))->other_case))\n434\t        {\n435\t        const uint32_t *pp = PRIV(ucd_caseless_sets) + ur->caseset;\n436\t\n437\t        /* When PCRE2_EXTRA_CASELESS_RESTRICT is set, ignore any caseless sets\n438\t        that start with an ASCII character. */\n439\t        if (caseless_restrict && *pp < 128) return -1;  /* No match */\n440\t\n441\t        for (;;)\n442\t          {\n443\t          if (c < *pp) return -1;  /* No match */\n444\t          if (c == *pp++) break;\n445\t          }\n446\t        }\n447\t      }\n448\t    }\n449\t  else\n450\t#endif\n451\t\n452\t  /* Not in UTF or UCP mode */\n453\t    {\n454\t    for (; length > 0; length--)\n455\t      {\n456\t      uint32_t cc, cp;\n457\t      if (eptr >= mb->end_subject) return 1;   /* Partial match */\n458\t      cc = *eptr;\n459\t      cp = *p;\n460\t      if (TABLE_GET(cp, mb->lcc, cp) != TABLE_GET(cc, mb->lcc, cc))\n461\t        return -1;  /* No match */\n462\t      p++;\n463\t      eptr++;\n464\t      }\n465\t    }\n466\t  }\n467\t\n468\t/* In the caseful case, we can just compare the code units, whether or not we\n469\tare in UTF and/or UCP mode. When partial matching, we have to do this unit by\n470\tunit. */\n471\t\n472\telse\n473\t  {\n474\t  if (mb->partial != 0)\n475\t    {\n476\t    for (; length > 0; length--)\n477\t      {\n478\t      if (eptr >= mb->end_subject) return 1;   /* Partial match */\n479\t      if (*p++ != *eptr++) return -1;  /* No match */\n480\t      }\n481\t    }\n482\t\n483\t  /* Not partial matching */\n484\t\n485\t  else\n486\t    {\n487\t    if ((PCRE2_SIZE)(mb->end_subject - eptr) < length ||\n488\t        memcmp(p, eptr, CU2BYTES(length)) != 0) return -1;  /* No match */\n489\t    eptr += length;\n490\t    }\n491\t  }\n492\t\n493\t*lengthptr = eptr - eptr_start;\n494\treturn 0;  /* Match */\n495\t}\n496\t\n497\t\n498\t\n499\t/*************************************************\n500\t*     Restore offsets after a recurse            *\n501\t*************************************************/\n502\t\n503\t/* This function restores the ovector values when\n504\ta recursive block reaches its end, and the triggering\n505\trecurse has and argument list.\n506\t\n507\tArguments:\n508\t  F           the current backtracking frame pointer\n509\t  P           the previous backtracking frame pointer\n510\t*/\n511\t\n512\tstatic void\n513\trecurse_update_offsets(heapframe *F, heapframe *P)\n514\t{\n515\tPCRE2_SIZE *dst = F->ovector;\n516\tPCRE2_SIZE *src = P->ovector;\n517\t/* The first bracket has offset 2, because\n518\toffset 0 is reserved for the full match. */\n519\tPCRE2_SIZE offset = 2;\n520\tPCRE2_SIZE offset_top = Foffset_top + 2;\n521\tPCRE2_SIZE diff;\n522\tPCRE2_SPTR ecode = Fecode;\n523\t\n524\tdo\n525\t  {\n526\t  diff = (GET2(ecode, 1) << 1) - offset;\n527\t  ecode += 1 + IMM2_SIZE;\n528\t\n529\t  if (offset + diff >= offset_top)\n530\t    {\n531\t    /* Some OP_CREF opcodes are not\n532\t    processed, they must be skipped. */\n533\t    while (*ecode == OP_CREF) ecode += 1 + IMM2_SIZE;\n534\t    break;\n535\t    }\n536\t\n537\t  if (diff == 2)\n538\t    {\n539\t    dst[0] = src[0];\n540\t    dst[1] = src[1];\n541\t    }\n542\t  else if (diff >= 4)\n543\t    memcpy(dst, src, diff * sizeof(PCRE2_SIZE));\n544\t\n545\t  /* Skip the unmodified entry. */\n546\t  diff += 2;\n547\t  offset += diff;\n548\t  dst += diff;\n549\t  src += diff;\n550\t  }\n551\twhile (*ecode == OP_CREF);\n552\t\n553\tdiff = offset_top - offset;\n554\tif (diff == 2)\n555\t  {\n556\t  dst[0] = src[0];\n557\t  dst[1] = src[1];\n558\t  }\n559\telse if (diff >= 4)\n560\t  memcpy(dst, src, diff * sizeof(PCRE2_SIZE));\n561\t\n562\tFecode = ecode;\n563\tFoffset_top = (offset <= P->offset_top) ? P->offset_top : (offset - 2);\n564\t}\n565\t\n566\t\n567\t\n568\t/******************************************************************************\n569\t*******************************************************************************\n570\t                   \"Recursion\" in the match() function\n571\t\n572\tThe original match() function was highly recursive, but this proved to be the\n573\tsource of a number of problems over the years, mostly because of the relatively\n574\tsmall system stacks that are commonly found. As new features were added to\n575\tpatterns, various kludges were invented to reduce the amount of stack used,\n576\tmaking the code hard to understand in places.\n577\t\n578\tA version did exist that used individual frames on the heap instead of calling\n579\tmatch() recursively, but this ran substantially slower. The current version is\n580\ta refactoring that uses a vector of frames to remember backtracking points.\n581\tThis runs no slower, and possibly even a bit faster than the original recursive\n582\timplementation.\n583\t\n584\tAt first, an initial vector of size START_FRAMES_SIZE (enough for maybe 50\n585\tframes) was allocated on the system stack. If this was not big enough, the heap\n586\twas used for a larger vector. However, it turns out that there are environments\n587\twhere taking as little as 20KiB from the system stack is an embarrassment.\n588\tAfter another refactoring, the heap is used exclusively, but a pointer the\n589\tframes vector and its size are cached in the match_data block, so that there is\n590\tno new memory allocation if the same match_data block is used for multiple\n591\tmatches (unless the frames vector has to be extended).\n592\t*******************************************************************************\n593\t******************************************************************************/\n594\t\n595\t\n596\t\n597\t\n598\t/*************************************************\n599\t*       Macros for the match() function          *\n600\t*************************************************/\n601\t\n602\t/* These macros pack up tests that are used for partial matching several times\n603\tin the code. The second one is used when we already know we are past the end of\n604\tthe subject. We set the \"hit end\" flag if the pointer is at the end of the\n605\tsubject and either (a) the pointer is past the earliest inspected character\n606\t(i.e. something has been matched, even if not part of the actual matched\n607\tstring), or (b) the pattern contains a lookbehind. These are the conditions for\n608\twhich adding more characters may allow the current match to continue.\n609\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01Fxcnhq5qRXVbZHDhAyK3Gk","session_id":"f08167af-b65d-45d4-8780-bbe04557b3d8","uuid":"92ee82fd-176d-4b0a-a694-b5f9d34e9a5c","timestamp":"2026-08-05T04:58:02.133Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Translate pcre2_match.c chunked"}
