{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"a4cda8c91bdd823d6","tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01MByBnnEu5LkGZfp5zwCNA4","status":"completed","output_file":"/tmp/claude-31072124/-tmp-harvest-translate-qnotxo-translated-rust/f08167af-b65d-45d4-8780-bbe04557b3d8/tasks/a4cda8c91bdd823d6.output","summary":"All external files are back to their original state. The translation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI translated `pcre2_match.c` (~8254 lines) to Rust at `/tmp/harvest-translate-qnotxo/translated_rust/src/pcre2_match.rs` (~5866 lines). The file compiles cleanly with zero errors and zero warnings, and passes a functional smoke test covering greedy/lazy quantifiers, backreferences, possessive/atomic groups, lookahead/lookbehind, word boundaries, anchors, alternation, and character classes.\n\n### Exported symbols (both `#[unsafe(no_mangle)] pub unsafe extern \"C\"`)\n- `pcre2_match_8(code, subject, length, start_offset, options, match_data, mcontext) -> c_int`\n- `pcre2_next_match_8(match_data, pstart_offset, poptions) -> c_int` (from `pcre2_match_next.c`, which lives in a separate C file; translated here as instructed)\n\nPer the spec I did NOT define `pcre2_get_startchar`/`pcre2_get_mark`. The `match()` engine and its statics are private `unsafe fn`s.\n\n### Key implementation approach\n- The C RMATCH/RRETURN heap-frame backtracking machine (computed-goto + `switch(Freturn_id)`) is modeled as a single `'machine: loop` over an `i32 state` variable. Positive states are the exact RMx resume ids from the C enum (RM1–RM39, RM100–RM103, RM200–RM224); negative/large states are internal machine points (MATCH_RECURSE, NEW_FRAME, MAINLOOP splits, goto-label states, and per-opcode backtrack loop heads).\n- `RMATCH!`/`RRETURN!`/`NEXT_OP!` are macros that set `state` and `continue 'machine`. Because Rust macro hygiene hides the outer loop label, the label is threaded through as a `$lbl:lifetime` macro parameter.\n- Every opcode case is reproduced faithfully (no stubs/skips), including all the `L*` frame-union local variables mapped onto `(*F).fields.*` and `byte1`/`byte2` via `fbyte1`/`fbyte2` helpers.\n- Helper functions `do_callout`, `match_ref`, `recurse_update_offsets`, plus `do_bumpalong` for next_match, are translated as private `unsafe fn`s.\n- Whitespace `HSPACE_CASES`/`VSPACE_CASES`, `UCD_ANY_I`/`UCD_FOLD_I_TURKISH`, `IS_NEWLINE`/`WAS_NEWLINE` (using `mb`), and the UTF char macros are implemented as local helpers/inline logic. `PCRE2_ASSERT`/`UNREACHABLE` are no-ops.\n\n### Notes\n- `PCRE2_ERROR_UTF8_ERR20` is not present in `pcre2_internal.rs`, so I defined it locally as `-22` (matching `pcre2_valid_utf.rs`'s local definition).\n- I did not add the `pub mod pcre2_match;` declaration to `lib.rs` (per instructions); the caller must register the module. I temporarily added it only to compile/test, then reverted `lib.rs`, `Cargo.toml`, and removed the temporary test.","usage":{"total_tokens":382227,"tool_uses":162,"duration_ms":3435806},"uuid":"5fc6c611-ec1d-4c4b-9b78-42d3b51319c5","session_id":"f08167af-b65d-45d4-8780-bbe04557b3d8"}
